# The owner's WhatsApp assistant on this computer (see assistant/README.md). Copy this file to assistant/.env and fill it in.
# assistant/.env holds a secret: git ignores it, keep it that way.

# The server's https address, and the same bridge token the server has (ASSISTANT_BRIDGE_TOKEN, 32+ characters).
ASSISTANT_SERVER_URL=https://your-server.example.com
ASSISTANT_BRIDGE_TOKEN=

# Optional.
# ASSISTANT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# The morning brief and the drafts (a reply, an email) run on a stronger model; off or empty: ASSISTANT_MODEL for them too.
# When the plan cannot use it, they run on ASSISTANT_MODEL for the rest of the day.
# ASSISTANT_WRITING_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
# ASSISTANT_TOOLS=WebSearch
# Adding WebFetch (ASSISTANT_TOOLS=WebSearch,WebFetch) is a risk: a web page or a forwarded message can make Pako fetch a link that
# carries your notes out to someone else's site, before any card asks you. Leave it off unless you need Pako to open pages.
# ASSISTANT_ROTATE_AFTER=30
# ASSISTANT_RUN_TIMEOUT_MS=180000
# CLAUDE_BIN=claude
# Voice notes (bash assistant/voice-setup.sh sets the model path):
# ASSISTANT_WHISPER_MODEL=
# ASSISTANT_WHISPER_LANG=auto
# The plan's quota (assistant/budget.ts): background runs a day, coalescing and unchanged windows in minutes, the effort of short verdicts,
# and how long your conversation's claude process stays up between messages.
# ASSISTANT_BACKGROUND_PER_DAY=40
# ASSISTANT_COALESCE_MIN=10
# ASSISTANT_UNCHANGED_MIN=120
# ASSISTANT_BACKGROUND_EFFORT=low
# ASSISTANT_WARM_MIN=10
# Pako's typed tools (assistant/mcp-server.ts): on when this Claude Code can load them; off for the tags alone.
# ASSISTANT_TYPED_TOOLS=off
# Updating itself (assistant/README.md, "Updates"): off unless set. With it on, only release tags signed by the pinned key are taken:
# an SSH allowed-signers file (path) or a GPG fingerprint. On with no signer pinned, it refuses and says so in its log.
# BRIDGE_AUTO_UPDATE=1
# BRIDGE_UPDATE_SIGNER=/Users/you/.config/pako/allowed_signers
